{"step_index":99,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:59:15Z","content":"All visual, interactive, and user experience enhancements for **NexusMobility — Smart City Eco-Logistics** have been completed:\n\n---\n\n### 🌟 Summary of Upgrades Delivered\n\n1. **Clean Header & Navigation**:\n   - Removed the \"Export Package (.ZIP)\" button.\n   - Streamlined down to primary controls: **\"Rush-Hour Simulation\"** and **\"Book Eco-Ride\"**.\n\n2. **Smooth 2D Micro-Lifting Hover**:\n   - Removed the heavy 3D perspective mouse-tracking tilt effect to eliminate card stuttering and dizziness.\n   - Replaced with a smooth 2D micro-lifting hover transition (`transform: translateY(-4px)` with soft emerald/slate drop-shadows).\n\n3. **Enhanced Spatial Map with Directional Flow & Station Indicators**:\n   - Directional chevron energy pulses animate along active corridors indicating transit flow from Origin to Destination.\n   - Distinct station node indicators with hub icons and clear zone metadata tags.\n\n4. **Animated Car Running Across Spatial Map Routes**:\n   - An electric transit vehicle drives smoothly along route corridor waypoints with glowing headlight beams and headlight trails upon route calculation or trip dispatch.\n   - Added a **\"Drive Route\"** action button in Tab 1 to re-run the simulation on demand.\n\n5. **Ambient Eco-Particle Background Layer**:\n   - Slow-drifting eco-leaves (with gentle sway and rotation) and soft electric blue energy nodes floating upwards across `#ambient-canvas`.\n\n6. **Friendly Eco-Mascot Character (\"EcoSprout\")**:\n   - An illustrated sprout mascot wearing aviator driving goggles and a leaf cap featured in empty state containers across the passenger queue, fleet directory, and active trips stream.\n\n7. **Professional Enterprise Alert Modals**:\n   - **Trip Dispatched Modal**: Displays trip reference, commuter name, driver partner, corridor alignment %, travel time, pooled fare, carbon offset, and a **\"View on Route Map\"** action button.\n   - **Trip Reversal Modal**: Details safe rollback confirmation, restored driver seat capacity, and commuter queue priority restoration.\n\n---\n\n### 📂 Direct File Access\n\n- 📄 **Application**: [index.html](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/index.html)\n- 🎨 **Styles & Animations**: [styles.css](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/styles.css)\n- ⚙️ **Transit Engine & Mascot Controller**: [app.js](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/app.js)\n- 📖 **Operating Manual**: [README.md](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/README.md)\n- 📋 **Walkthrough Summary**: [walkthrough.md](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/walkthrough.md)\n\nOpen [index.html](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/index.html) in your browser to experience the smooth 2D hover elevation, animated car transit simulation on the 3D map, ambient background particles, and EcoSprout mascot!"}
{"step_index":100,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:06:06Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\n# TASK: Create C++ Backend Server for NexusMobility Eco-Logistics Platform\r\n\r\n## Objective\r\nConvert the front-end state engine (`app.js`) of the NexusMobility application into a modern, thread-safe C++ REST API server. The C++ backend will handle pathfinding algorithms, data structures (circular buffers, queues, priority matching), trip dispatching, and auditing, while serving JSON responses to the frontend.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🛠️ Architecture & Technical Stack\r\n- **Language Standard**: Modern C++20 / C++17\r\n- **HTTP/REST Framework**: Crow C++ (or CrowCpp / Pistache / httplib)\r\n- **JSON Serialization**: `nlohmann/json`\r\n- **Build System**: CMake (Minimum version 3.16)\r\n- **Data Structures**:\r\n  - `std::vector` and adjacency lists for graph routing\r\n  - Priority Queue / Min-Heap for Dijkstra's shortest path\r\n  - Ring Buffer / Circular Queue (`std::array` or `std::vector` with head/tail pointers) for the 5-Slot Priority Standby Lounge\r\n  - Thread-safe FIFO `std::queue` for the Commuter Dispatch Pipeline\r\n  - `std::stack` or custom vector deque for the Reversal Audit Log\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 📋 Core Modules to Implement in C++\r\n\r\n### 1. Data Models (`Models.hpp`)\r\nDefine clean C++ structs with standard serialization to JSON:\r\n- `Station`: `id` (string), `name` (string), `x` (double), `y` (double), `z` (double), `zone` (string), `icon` (string)\r\n- `Corridor`: `u` (string), `v` (string), `distance` (double)\r\n- `Passenger`: `id` (string), `name` (string), `pickup` (string), `drop` (string), `requestedAt` (string), `status` (string)\r\n- `Driver`: `id` (int), `name` (string), `station` (string), `seats` (int), `originalSeats` (int), `tripsCompleted` (int)\r\n- `Trip`: `tripRef` (string), `passenger` (Passenger), `driverId` (int), `driverName` (string), `corridorPath` (vector<string>), `distance` (double), `time` (int), `fare` (double), `co2Saved` (double), `matchScore` (int), `dispatchedAt` (string)\r\n- `AuditAction`: `type` (string), `tripRef` (string), `driverId` (int), `passenger` (Passenger), `trip` (Trip)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 2. Core Engine Logic (`NexusEngine.hpp` / `NexusEngine.cpp`)\r\nImplement a thread-safe singleton or managed object containing:\r\n\r\n#### A. Graph Routing & Math Engine\r\n- **`findOptimalEcoRoute(startId, endId, commuterDensity)`**:\r\n  - Run **Dijkstra's Shortest Path Algorithm** on the station adjacency graph.\r\n  - Compute total distance ($\\text{km}$), estimated time ($\\text{mins} = \\text{round}(\\text{distance} \\times 2.2)$).\r\n  - Compute CO₂ offset saved ($0.171 \\times \\text{distance} \\times (0.8 + \\text{density} \\times 0.4)$).\r\n  - Compute pooled fare calculation ($[4.0 + \\text{distance} \\times 1.5 \\times (1 + (\\text{density} - 1) \\times 0.25)] / \\text{density}$).\r\n\r\n#### B. Commuter Pipeline Queue\r\n- `std::queue<Passenger> dispatchStream`\r\n- Methods: `submitRideRequest()`, `dequeueNextRequest()`\r\n\r\n#### C. Fixed 5-Slot Standby Ring Buffer\r\n- Fixed Capacity Array of size 5 (`std::array<std::optional<Passenger>, 5>`)\r\n- Circular array pointer indexing (`front`, `rear`, `count`)\r\n- Methods: `pushToStandby()`, `popFromStandby()`\r\n\r\n#### D. Fleet Management & Dispatch Matching\r\n- `std::vector<Driver> fleetPartners`\r\n- `std::vector<Trip> activeTrips`\r\n- Methods:\r\n  - `onboardDriver(name, station, seats)`\r\n  - `dispatchSharedTrip(...)`: Matches commuter with driver, decrements seats, increments trip counter, pushes trip to `activeTrips`, and records an audit action.\r\n  - `cancelTrip(tripRef)`\r\n\r\n#### E. Reversal Audit Log\r\n- `std::vector<AuditAction> reversalAuditLog` (Acts as LIFO Rollback Stack)\r\n- Method: `revertLatestConfirmation()`: Reverts the last dispatched trip, restores the passenger to the head of the dispatch queue, and restores driver seat capacity.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🚀 API Endpoint Specifications\r\n\r\nExpose the following JSON API routes via Crow C++ HTTP server listening on port `8080`:\r\n\r\n| HTTP Method | Route | Description |\r\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\r\n| `GET` | `/api/stations` | List all network transit stations |\r\n| `POST` | `/api/route/calculate` | Calculate optimal route (`{ \"origin\": \"ALPHA\", \"destination\": \"HORIZON\", \"density\": 2 }`) |\r\n| `POST` | `/api/passengers/request` | Submit new ride request (`{ \"name\": \"...\", \"pickup\": \"...\", \"drop\": \"...\" }`) |\r\n| `POST` | `/api/passengers/dequeue` | Dequeue front passenger from pipeline |\r\n| `POST` | `/api/standby/push` | Move passenger to 5-slot priority standby ring buffer |\r\n| `POST` | `/api/standby/pop` | Seat passenger from standby ring buffer |\r\n| `POST` | `/api/drivers/on\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-20T11:36:06+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
